#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096477 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef0d732d-f50b-5179-9a77-1378a84173ac" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Vertically Reflected Function"}] :question/id #uuid "92bc7054-dfe9-539d-a27d-33207aade624" :question/math-academy-id "e-4976" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Sketch the graph of $y=-f(x)$.\n\n![](images/ed/edd8085cc401a9dec16e03357f31ded4598d8bcfd19ed2e9c06e9cc64d5e4ea3.png)" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the graph of $y=−f(x)$ from $y=f(x)$, we need to reflect the graph over the $x$-axis. The resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/c9/c978264dfc9cc8f492c3b984ed93273f508c6a25fb82592dd70c4dfe642a8b19.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096478 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7540cdde-f84f-5be9-8ffa-f2e9c6ea59ff" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Point on a Vertically Reflected Function"}] :question/id #uuid "37244ac9-1237-5a8c-8d9b-fee1355aa666" :question/math-academy-id "e-4978" :question/problem "The point $P$ with coordinates $(2, -1)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x)$. Which point must lie on the graph of $y= -f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The transformation $y=-f(x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(2, -1)$ lies $1$ unit *below* the $x$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected $1$ unit *above* the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/5f/5fc11d4ceb5ce0a1c9e7cd95fed19a07b3b3a78185f7dd8131f069bcdcc4bb1a.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point $(2,1)$ must lie on the graph of $y=-f(x).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef0d732d-f50b-5179-9a77-1378a84173ac" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Vertically Reflected Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [